original_text:
@jaclynmdiaz the central question you must explore is this:

Gun control laws are supposedly enacted to prevent violence by criminals and lunatics, but only sane, law abiding people follow the laws.  

When do criminals and lunatics care about laws?  By definition, they don't.

mirror_text:
@jaclynmdiaz the central question you must explore is this:

Guns are supposedly owned by law-abiding citizens for self-defense, but they keep ending up in the hands of criminals and killing innocent people.

When do thoughts and prayers ever stop a bullet? By definition, they don't.
